</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The log-probabilities in brackets are full-vocabulary probabilities; only the weighting factor <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{p}_{S,\mathrm{old}}^{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>old</mi></mrow><mi>A</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{p}_{S,\mathrm{old}}^{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is normalized over <math id="S2.SS6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. The candidate sets and advantages are computed from the rollout policy and held fixed during the subsequent update.</p>
