<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Mathematical reasoning.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate three student–teacher pairs spanning different model sizes and reasoning modes. The first pair uses Qwen3-1.7B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Team, 2025</a>)</cite> in non-thinking mode as the student and Qwen3-4B-Non-Thinking-RL-Math <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2026a</a>)</cite> as the teacher. The other two pairs use DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-1.5B and DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, paired with JustRL-DeepSeek-1.5B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">He et al., 2025a</a>)</cite> and Skywork-OR1-Math-7B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">He et al., 2025b</a>)</cite>, respectively. These pairs cover both non-thinking and reasoning models, including settings where the student and teacher have the same parameter count but differ in post-training.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Code generation.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate Qwen3-4B in non-thinking mode with two teachers: Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507 and Qwen3-30B-A3B-Instruct-2507 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Team, 2025</a>)</cite>. This comparison examines distillation from different teachers while keeping the initial student fixed. We additionally evaluate Qwen2.5-Coder-3B-Instruct with Qwen2.5-Coder-32B-Instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hui et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, extending the evaluation to a code-specialized model family.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Agentic tasks and model roles.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For agentic tasks, we use Qwen3-4B as the student and Qwen3-4B-Thinking-2507 as the teacher, both configured in non-thinking mode. In our default setup, the question synthesizer is initialized as an independent copy of the corresponding student. During synthesizer optimization, the scoring student and teacher remain frozen; downstream OPD starts from the original student parameters and updates only the student. We separately examine teacher-initialized synthesizers in the synthesizer-initialization ablation. Exact checkpoint identifiers and inference configurations are provided in the appendix.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Auxiliary models.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For agentic tasks, we use GPT-4o-mini <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">OpenAI, 2024</a>)</cite> as the user simulator and judge. For semantic deduplication of the generated question bank, we use a frozen Qwen3-Embedding-4B model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2025</a>)</cite> only after synthesizer training. It is not used to compute training-time diversity rewards or optimize the synthesizer. These auxiliary models remain fixed throughout our experiments.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Baselines</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compare <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">A2D</span> with the following baselines and reference models: (1) <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Student and Teacher</span>: the initial student before distillation and its corresponding teacher, which establish the starting performance and the reference for teacher-gap recovery; (2) <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Vanilla OPD</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2026b</a>)</cite>: on-policy distillation using the original question bank for each domain, DAPO-17k-Math <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yu et al., 2025</a>)</cite> for mathematical reasoning, OpenCodeReasoning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ahmad et al., 2025</a>)</cite> for code generation, and the official <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-Bench training set <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Barrès et al., 2025</a>)</cite> for agentic tasks—where the student generates responses and the teacher provides token-level supervision on student-generated prefixes, serving as the standard real-data reference; (3) <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Student-Generated OPD</span>: OPD using questions sampled directly from the initial student without synthesizer optimization, evaluating whether explicitly training the question-generation policy provides benefits beyond the student’s existing generation capability; (4) <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">KL-Filtered OPD</span>: OPD using the 20% of real questions with the highest teacher–student KL disagreement, testing whether retaining high-disagreement questions alone provides effective distillation data;</p>
</div>
