<section id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Combining with filtering and OPD variants</h4>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">A2D</span> learns a question distribution for a target student–teacher pair, while filtering determines which sampled questions are retained and the downstream OPD procedure determines how teacher supervision updates the student. These operations act at different stages of the pipeline. Consequently, learned question generation can be followed by additional filtering or selection rules, and the resulting synthetic bank can be used by alternative distillation procedures that accept prompt-only datasets. Our format filtering and deduplication already illustrate this separation: they curate the synthesizer’s outputs before those questions are used for OPD.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The learning-value reward nevertheless connects prompt optimization to the downstream distillation procedure. Our support-aware score is designed around teacher supervision on the student’s candidate support. A procedure using a different divergence, candidate support, or supervision allocation rule may benefit from a corresponding adaptation of the generation reward. We therefore view <span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">A2D</span> as a modular approach to constructing distillation prompts, with the effectiveness of any particular combination depending on how well the generation objective matches the downstream learning signal. Exploring such combinations is a natural direction for future work.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F10" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_floatleft" style="width:47%;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2610.27450v1/exp2b_heatmap.svg" id="A1.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:229/154;" width="229" height="154"></object>
